On-device AI refers to a type of AI technology that runs locally on a device, such as a smartphone or tablet, instead of relying on cloud services. It means the AI model is trained and optimized directly on the device itself, without needing to connect to the internet or cloud. This approach allows for real-time performance and data privacy, as the model doesn't require external data or network connectivity.

